  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 械\ntitle: machine; fetter\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-4, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 11\nradical: 木\nradicalNumber: 75\nonyomi: [カイ]\nkunyomi: [かせ]\ndistractors: [校, 式, 枚]\n---\n\n# 械 — machine; fetter\n\n**Strokes:** 11 · **Key (radical):** 木 (no. 75) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n械 occurs in words about machinery or implements, such as 機械 きかい, machine. The separate native word 械 かせ names shackles or fetters; this written form is marked rare in the inspected dictionary.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** Notice 木 beside the 戒-shaped right side and imagine a wooden restraint. This is a modern-shape mnemonic, not a historical or phonetic analysis.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| カイ | on | [機械](../words/機械.md) きかい - machine; mechanism |\n| かせ | kun | 械 かせ - shackles; fetters (rare kanji spelling) |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [機械](../words/機械.md) きかい - machine; mechanism\n- [器械](../words/機械.md) きかい - instrument; apparatus (related spelling taught in the same article)\n\n## Notes\n\n- JMdict lists 枷 and 械 in the かせ entry and marks 械 as a rare kanji spelling. That is a spelling qualification, not evidence that かせ is a rare pronunciation.\n- The linked 機械 article distinguishes a machine or mechanism from 器械 きかい, an instrument or apparatus. An identical reading does not make their usual contexts identical.\n- Compare [校](校.md), school, and [枚](枚.md), a flat-object counter. The right-hand strokes distinguish these 木-left characters.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1220810, 1568000.\n",
